.TH "PB-TUNNEL-POLICY-GET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-policy-get - Show an on-demand port policy


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel policy get <policy> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show an on-demand port policy

.PP
Show one on-demand port policy, including its target and authorization state. Use its identity and generation for a deliberate revoke.

.PP
An on-demand policy authorizes an exact machine port for private or team access. A policy does not publish a public URL or grant every port on the device. Revocation fences subsequent activation.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for get

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel-policy(1)\fP
